<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Christopher Columbus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1451–<a href="/years/1506">1506</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Columbus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Christopher Columbus was a Genoese navigator whose voyage of 1492, funded by the Castilian crown, reached the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>. His voyages initiated Spanish colonisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> and the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a>. He sought a western route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, inspired in part by accounts of the court of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> such as that of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-polo">Marco Polo</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="Christopher Columbus" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sebastiano del Piombo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_a_Man,_Said_to_be_Christopher_Columbus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
